# =============================================================================
# Backend Environment — KEY-NAME TEMPLATE
# This file documents configuration KEY NAMES and the channels that supply
# values. It is a reference, not a source: a `.env` file is NOT one of the
# host's configuration providers, so neither this file nor a copy of it is
# ever read at runtime.
#
# Supply values through a provider the host actually reads:
#   local development  →  dotnet user-secrets (see the sections below)
#   deployment         →  host environment variables
# NEVER commit real secrets
# =============================================================================

# ─── Database (PostgreSQL via WSL Docker) ───────────────────────────────────
ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection=Host=localhost;Port=5433;Database=dcacti_db;Username=dcacti;Password=dcacti_dev_password;Include Error Detail=true

# ─── Redis (via WSL Docker) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
ConnectionStrings__Redis=localhost:6379

# ─── Application session signing key (ADR-015 D10) ──────────────────────────
# REQUIRED: the host reads this during composition and refuses to start without
# it. It never generates, defaults, or substitutes a key, and it never echoes
# the value back (ApplicationSessionSigningKeys.CreateHmacKey).
#
# ADR-015 D10 forbids the secret in appsettings.json,
# appsettings.Development.json, .env.example, source code, a test fixture, a log
# line, or any committed artifact. Supply it locally from the user-secrets store
# or from a host environment variable — the project has a UserSecretsId for
# exactly this, and neither channel writes a secret into the working tree:
#
#   dotnet user-secrets --project src/backend/GameServer.Api set "ApplicationSession:CurrentKey:Secret" "<at least 32 random bytes>"
#   dotnet user-secrets --project src/backend/GameServer.Api set "ApplicationSession:CurrentKey:KeyId" "dev-1"
#
# The store is read in the Development environment only (an ASP.NET Core default
# configuration provider). A `.env` file is not one of the host's providers: if
# you keep values in one locally, export them into the environment instead.
#
# The key NAMES below are the contract (ApplicationSessionOptions). They carry
# key identifiers and secret values — never put a real value in this file.
#
#   ApplicationSession__CurrentKey__Secret    the HS256 secret (>= 32 bytes)
#   ApplicationSession__CurrentKey__KeyId     the `kid` naming that key (D11)
#   ApplicationSession__PreviousKey__Secret   only during a rotation overlap
#   ApplicationSession__PreviousKey__KeyId    only during a rotation overlap

# ─── CORS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Cors__AllowedOrigins__0=http://localhost:5173
Cors__AllowedOrigins__1=https://localhost:5173

# ─── ASP.NET Core ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development
ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://localhost:5000
